  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 29,
    "summary": "When the wicked rule, the people mourn—The righteous consider the cause of the poor—A fool speaks all that is in his mind—Where there is no vision, the people perish.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "He, that being often reproved hardeneth his neck, shall suddenly be destroyed, and that without remedy.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 102,
            "text": "Prov. 6:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When the righteous are in authority, the people rejoice: but when the wicked beareth rule, the people mourn.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Governments."
          },
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "Mosiah 5:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "TG Wickedness."
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "TG Authority; Leadership; Tyranny."
          },
          {
            "start": 102,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "Mosiah 7:23 (22–23); D&C 98:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso loveth wisdom rejoiceth his father: but he that keepeth company with harlots spendeth his substance.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "Mosiah 11:4 (2–4)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 95
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The king by judgment establisheth the land: but he that receiveth gifts overthroweth it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man that flattereth his neighbour spreadeth a net for his feet.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "Alma 46:5 (4–35)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In the transgression of an evil man there is a snare: but the righteous doth sing and rejoice.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG Transgress."
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "Alma 12:6; D&C 10:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The righteous considereth the cause of the poor: but the wicked regardeth not to know it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 52
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 89
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Scornful men bring a city into a snare: but wise men turn away wrath.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If a wise man contendeth with a foolish man, whether he rage or laugh, there is no rest.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 79
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The bloodthirsty hate the upright: but the just seek his soul.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Hel. 16:2; Ether 13:22 (13–15, 22)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A fool uttereth all his mind: but a wise man keepeth it in till afterwards.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "D&C 63:64."
          },
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "TG Mind."
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "Prov. 17:28 (27–28)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If a ruler hearken to lies, all his servants are wicked.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The poor and the deceitful man meet together: the Lord lighteneth both their eyes.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The king that faithfully judgeth the poor, his throne shall be established for ever.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Kings, Earthly."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The rod and reproof give wisdom: but a child left to himself bringeth his mother to shame.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "Prov. 13:24."
          },
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "TG Chastening; Reproof."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "TG Family, Children, Responsibilities toward."
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Motherhood."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "TG Shame."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When the wicked are multiplied, transgression increaseth: but the righteous shall see their fall.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Correct thy son, and he shall give thee rest; yea, he shall give delight unto thy soul.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Where there is no vision, the people perish: but he that keepeth the law, happy is he.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Revelation; Vision."
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of Individuals."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "Luke 11:28."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "Prov. 28:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Happiness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A servant will not be corrected by words: for though he understand he will not answer.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Seest thou a man that is hasty in his words? there is more hope of a fool than of him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "TG Haste; Rashness."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "Prov. 26:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 24
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that delicately bringeth up his servant from a child shall have him become his son at the length.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 81
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "An angry man stirreth up strife, and a furious man aboundeth in transgression.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "Eccl. 7:9; Matt. 5:22."
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "TG Strife."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man’s pride shall bring him low: but honour shall uphold the humble in spirit.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Prov. 17:19; 18:12; Hel. 12:5 (1–5)."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Humility."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso is partner with a thief hateth his own soul: he heareth cursing, and bewrayeth it not.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Hate."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 87
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The fear of man bringeth a snare: but whoso putteth his trust in the Lord shall be safe.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "John 12:42 (42–43); 19:38. TG Peer Influence."
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 61,
            "text": "TG Trust in God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Many seek the ruler’s favour; but every man’s judgment cometh from the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Prov. 19:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 39
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "An unjust man is an abomination to the just: and he that is upright in the way is abomination to the wicked.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "1 Ne. 15:36."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 59
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 81
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
